From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:43:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: add the MT6797 CONSYS controller

The MT6797 Bluetooth controller has no port of its own. Its HCI packets travel as
H:4 over STP task 0 on the CONSYS link, not aligned with STP frames.

Add an HCI driver on that link. Opening the device attaches to the link and turns
the function on, and closing reverses it. Loading the module opens the device once:
registering an HCI device makes the core run its setup stage and close the device
about 2 s later. That stage starts no inquiry, page or scan.

Reassembly runs in the link's interrupt handler and hands whole packets to a work
item. It never refuses a frame, because a refusal stops the link for every CONSYS
client, Wi-Fi's firmware included. A malformed stream or a failed allocation drops
only Bluetooth: the rest of the stream is ignored and the core gets a hardware
error, which reopens the device.

The two radio parameters Gemian's driver sends on this chip are behind the
gemian_radio parameter, off by default, since they change radio settings that no
mainline run has changed. The vendor's sleep timeout is left out, since nothing
here puts the chip to sleep or wakes it.

The controller's own address is used. set_bdaddr is there for a board whose address
is unusable.
---
 drivers/bluetooth/Kconfig       |  10 ++
 drivers/bluetooth/Makefile      |   1 +
 drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797-h4.h |  87 ++++++++++++
 drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797.c    | 227 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 325 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797-h4.h
 create mode 100644 drivers/bluetooth/btmt6797.c

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/Kconfig b/drivers/bluetooth/Kconfig
index c5d45cf91..42a68f72e 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/Kconfig
@@ -438,6 +438,16 @@ config BT_MTKSDIO
 	  Say Y here to compile support for MediaTek Bluetooth SDIO devices
 	  into the kernel or say M to compile it as module (btmtksdio).
 
+config BT_MT6797
+	tristate "MediaTek MT6797 CONSYS Bluetooth"
+	depends on MTK_MT6797_CONSYS
+	help
+	  Say Y here for the Bluetooth controller inside the MT6797 connectivity
+	  subsystem. Its HCI packets travel over the CONSYS STP link.
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will
+	  be called btmt6797.
+
 config BT_MTKUART
 	tristate "MediaTek HCI UART driver"
 	depends on BT_HCIUART
diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/Makefile b/drivers/bluetooth/Makefile
index 81856512d..c2f320cdd 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/Makefile
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_BT_MRVL)		+= btmrvl.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_BT_MRVL_SDIO)	+= btmrvl_sdio.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_BT_MTKSDIO)	+= btmtksdio.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_BT_MTKUART)	+= btmtkuart.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_BT_MT6797)		+= btmt6797.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_BT_QCOMSMD)	+= btqcomsmd.o
